~ rubble
do disable_movement()
The rubble is in the way. Whatever is behind it, it stays behind it for now.
do enable_movement()
=> END

~ sealed
do disable_movement()
Cold air moves against your face. The passage slopes down, further than it has any right to.
Whatever is waiting down there isn't ready for you yet.
do enable_movement()
=> END

~ enter
do disable_movement()
The dark resolves into a corridor. You go down.
do enable_movement()
=> END
